function is_anagram($str1, $str2) {
  // Remove any spaces and punctuation from the input strings
  $str1 = preg_replace('/[^A-Za-z0-9]/', '', strtolower($str1));
  $str2 = preg_replace('/[^A-Za-z0-9]/', '', strtolower($str2));

  // Convert the input strings into arrays of characters
  $arr1 = str_split($str1);
  $arr2 = str_split($str2);

  // Sort the arrays of characters
  sort($arr1);
  sort($arr2);

  // Check if the sorted arrays of characters are equal
  return ($arr1 === $arr2);
}
```

This function first removes any spaces and punctuation from the input strings using a regular expression. It then converts the input strings into arrays of characters using the `str_split()` function. The arrays are sorted using the `sort()` function. Finally, the function checks if the sorted arrays are equal using the identity operator `===`.

