AVL tree is a self-balancing binary search tree. The balance factor is maintained for each node of the tree which is equal to the difference between the height of the left sub-tree and the right sub-tree.

The insert() and delete() operations in AVL tree are similar to those in any other binary search tree. However, the main difference lies in the rebalancing of the AVL tree whenever the height difference becomes greater than 1.

The AVL tree has the following property:
- For any node in the tree, the height difference between its left and right sub-trees is at most 1.

To ensure that the AVL tree remains balanced, we perform the following rotations when the height difference becomes greater than 1:
- Left-Left Rotation
- Right-Right Rotation
- Left-Right Rotation
- Right-Left Rotation

The search() operation is similar to that in any other binary search tree.

The inorder(), preorder(), and postorder() traversal operations are also similar to those in any other binary tree.

The implementation of AVL tree is as follows:

```
public class AVLTree {

    private class Node {
        int key;
        int height;
        Node left;
        Node right;

        Node(int key) {
            this.key = key;
            height = 1;
        }
    }

    private Node root;

    public void insert(int key) {
        root = insert(root, key);
    }

    private Node insert(Node node, int key) {
        if (node == null) {
            return new Node(key);
        }

        if (key < node.key) {
            node.left = insert(node.left, key);
        } else if (key > node.key) {
            node.right = insert(node.right, key);
        } else {
            return node; // key already exists
        }

        node.height = 1 + Math.max(getHeight(node.left), getHeight(node.right));

        int balance = getBalance(node);

        // Left-Left Rotation
        if (balance > 1 && key < node.left.key) {
            return rightRotate(node);
        }

        // Right-Right Rotation
        if (balance < -1 && key > node.right.key) {
            return leftRotate(node);
        }

        // Left-Right Rotation
        if (balance > 1 && key > node.left.key) {
            node.left = leftRotate(node.left);
            return rightRotate(node);
